=== STEP 3: log2|C| COMPUTATION ===

Challenge set C = { c in R_q : deg(c) < n, exactly tau coefficients are +/-1, rest zero }
|C| = C(n, tau) * 2^tau   (binomial coefficient * sign choices)
log2|C| = log2(C(n, tau)) + tau

Parameters: n=256, tau=60 (SAME for all four parameter sets)

C(256, 60) = 202929899521004920281576448432233382754299099020348543566400
log2(C(256, 60)) = 197.0147 bits   (computed: Python math.comb() + math.log2())
log2|C| = 197.0147 + 60 = 257.0147 bits

Note: tau=60 is IDENTICAL for all four TCHES 2018 parameter sets.
Therefore log2|C| = 257.01 bits for ALL sets (weak, medium, recommended, very_high).

=== STEP 4: SELFTARGETMSIS ESTIMATE (APPLYING SPECIFICATION FORMULA) ===

Specification formula: cost_SelfTargetMSIS = cost_MSIS + log2|C|

Note on formula provenance:
  This formula is from IDEA-20260805-3f7ab2, NOT from KN-LIT-056.
  KN-LIT-056 Appendix C.3 says: "best known attack [on SelfTargetMSIS] involves
  either breaking the security of H or solving the MSISk,l+1,zeta problem for
  [A | t0]." In the paper's analysis, SelfTargetMSIS ~ MSIS (comparable cost).
  The formula treats log2|C| as an additive cost component (hash programmability);
  this interpretation may differ from the paper's analysis.

Results (all applying classical cost_MSIS from Table 2):
  weak:        cost_MSIS=68 + log2|C|=257.01 = 325.01 bits
  medium:      cost_MSIS=103 + log2|C|=257.01 = 360.01 bits
  recommended: cost_MSIS=138 + log2|C|=257.01 = 395.01 bits
  very_high:   cost_MSIS=176 + log2|C|=257.01 = 433.01 bits

Discrepancy (formula vs paper MSIS estimate):
  All four sets: +257.01 bits (formula gives HIGHER estimate than MSIS alone)
  This is the log2|C| component. The formula produces estimates well above
  the MSIS estimates in Table 2.

Dominant component at all parameter sets: log2|C| (257 bits) >> cost_MSIS (68-176 bits)

